    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0306" n="306" xml:id="pg306"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr.
                            Clay</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 9, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Appleton’s despatch of May 22, (June
                    3,) No. 18, has been received.</p>
                <p>It contains the orders in admiralty on the subject of the treatment of American
                    vessels during the present condition of our internal affairs.</p>
                <p>The subject seems to call for no special instruction to you, except to express to
                    the Russian government the satisfaction which this government feels in regard to
                    the conduct and friendly action of the Emperor.</p>
                <p>Mr. Appleton is now with us, and we are deriving much profit from the information
                    he gives. We learn your high appreciation of his conduct in his mission with
                    pleasure.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius M. Clay</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
